OK, so let me explain how the weekly tasks are organised. The watering team, as you might expect, usually looks after the vegetable beds; they're the thirstiest part of the site. Weeding tends to happen along the glasshouse rows, where the paths get overgrown. Composting is a steady job, and it all ends up at the corner of the site, near the delivery gate. Pruning is more seasonal — we save it for the flower borders each autumn, when the roses need cutting back. And harvesting, as the name suggests, is concentrated in the herb garden towards the end of summer, when the herbs are at their best.
